 double-digit summer leads", "$10M outside infusion for Demuth in the most expensive governor's race in state history"], "rationale": "Klobuchar leads every recent poll by two to ten points, holds an overwhelming money and recognition advantage in an open seat, and raters and markets alike place the race firmly in the Democratic column. A modest September tightening and fresh outside spending for Demuth keep this short of Safe, but the evidence supports a high-single-digit Democratic margin.", "watch": "The October 21 debate and the Demuth-aligned PAC's $10 million war chest could further narrow the race if Klobuchar's September polling slide continues.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open governor's race pits Senator Amy Klobuchar against state Representative Lisa Demuth after Tim Walz chose not to seek another term. Klobuchar enters with deep name recognition, a roughly $7 million war chest against Demuth's half-million, and a lead in every public poll this fall, though her margin has narrowed from double digits in midsummer to between two and ten points in September surveys. Rating outlets uniformly place the race in the Democratic column, from Likely to Solid D, and prediction markets price her chances around 93 to 95 percent.\n\nDemuth has consolidated Republican support and benefits from a $10 million infusion to an allied PAC in what has become the most expensive governor's race in state history. Still, Minnesota's modest Democratic lean and Klobuchar's durable standing leave her the clear favorite heading into the October 21 debate.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"da